    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "212637de_9164adb2",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-21T15:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think adding a RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_START and RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_END would be good to add into the flow.\n\nThis would allow the EC to track a timeout on the overall process and take recovery actions in the event the AP crashes during this process.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 463,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 463,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "3e9980ed8fafc8037698044368344073babc09d6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d80fd6b6_38a4385b",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-21T19:09:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The update flow has two parts, 1. AP scan retimers during boot up, flow is suspend-\u003e...resume. 2. if user decides doing firmware update, AP will start the flow suspend-\u003e...-\u003eresume again. Yes, it\u0027s possible PD is suspended but AP has problem and couldn\u0027t tell EC to resume. To have recovery process, how about if EC receives Operation SUSPEND_PD, internally EC set the flag RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_START, and once receives resume, set the flag RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_END for EC can track timeout?",
      "parentUuid": "212637de_9164adb2",
